{White absent ill without notice - defaulted by arbiter. "Local hopes rested
on the shoulders of 19-year-old John Emms, who started strongly with 2(2).
Unfortunately he defaulted in round 3 (against me) after breaking his wrist in
a football match. John attempted to inform the organisers of his predicament
but was unable to get through. In a rather delicate situation the controller
decided that the default should stand, reasoning that he had not made
sufficient effort to reach them. Of course, this unfortunate incident put paid
to John’s norm chances." (Geoff Lawton, BCM, March 1987, p112)}  0-1

